        "title": "Growing Wild, serving Marina Del Rey, CA",
        "content": "<p>Located a few miles from LAX, is the charming neighborhood of <a href=\"https://visitmdr.com/\">Marina del Rey</a>. It is renowned for its beautiful beaches, bike paths, and the world's largest man-made small craft harbor - the Marina Del Rey Marina. Washington Boulevard borders Marina del Rey’s northern perimeter, while <a href=\"https://www.culvercity.org/Explore/Ballona-Creek\">Ballona Creek</a> borders the southern perimeter. Head east to find Lincoln Boulevard or go west to find Via Dolce. The colorful buildings at <a href=\"https://visitmdr.com/place/fishermans-village\">Fisherman's Village</a> greatly add to its beauty. Concerts featuring talented musicians are often held at <a href=\"https://chacepark.com/\">Burton Chace Park</a></p><p>The most popular Growing Wild floral arrangements among residents are our Spring Fling, White Loveliness, and Joyous flowers. Our seasoned designers will be happy to make romantic, floral centerpieces for anniversary celebrations held at Fisherman's Village restaurants. Customers at the Pacific Yacht Club, California Yacht Club, UCLA Aquatic Center, and the Ritz Carlton at the Marina Del Rey Marina rely on us frequently for birthday bouquets and special event floral decorations. Buy the stunning Simple Summer bouquet on our website now for concert performers at Burton Chace Park.</p>",
